Source ROM: targets/msm8930-r1.2/pbl.bin
  sha256 c1a7d8ffc9a3b9581953107861e61d9d7d9b9b2c5dafd929571446614884f92e
  (identical to the dump recorded in TARGETID-LOADER-NOTES.md, pbl-lab,
  acquired 2026-10-01 from Samsung Galaxy Express GT-I8730, MSM8930 soc_id 116 rev 1.2,
  read via /dev/mem at physical 0x0, two byte-identical reads)

Reconstructed range: 0x4554..0x45FF inclusive (172 bytes = 43 ARM words).
Method: manual instruction transcription from the disassembled ROM slice
  (capstone 5.0.x listing from tools/rom.py disasm + cross-checked with pbl-lab
  idx.raw dumps), assembled with arm-none-eabi-as -mcpu=arm7tdmi -EL and linked
  at -Ttext=0x4554; objcopy -O binary compared whole-file against
  ROM[0x4554:0x4600]. No trimming, masking or post-patch of the comparison.

Non-relocatable encodings pinned as .word in the source, by ROM evidence:
  .word 0xEB000142  @ 0x45a8: bl 0x4ab8 (bignum context alloc)
  .word 0xEBFFF7C3  @ 0x45c8: bl 0x24dc (byte accessor used for every byte load)
  .word 0xDA000150  @ 0x4570: ble 0x4ab8 (len<=0 path calls alloc(1,0) directly)
  .word 0xA25CC001  @ 0x4594: subsge ip, ip, #1 (limb-count overflow decrement)
  .word 0xEAFFFFEE  @ 0x45fc: b return_zero (tail-duplicated epilogue)
Reason: gas -mcpu=arm7tdmi emits veneers for absolute branches to externally
  defined absolute symbols; every other encoding folds strictly from source.

Behaviour significance (from the pbl-lab analysis of the same ROM):
  - function consumes (ptr r0, byte len r1), ingesting len bytes into limb
    storage; returns NULL when the ceil(len/4) limb count exceeds 0x100 limbs
    (0x45b8 return_zero path; ip decrement at 0x4594).
  - len == 0 returns a fresh count-0 bignum, NOT an error (0x4564..0x4570).
  - The caller chain (per-certificate verify at 0xbdac per-row state blocks
    [fp+0x2f4]/[fp+0x2f8]; image-signature verify at 0xf840) feeds the byte
    count parsed from the image and relies on this loader verbatim.
  - Negative gate: ROM slice compares equal only to the exact reconstruction.

